{"assets":["/statement-assets/0a8c06923497c004271bd233089f67784b07aa282bb72b78ada1ac395fec1ebb.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"527","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Clique Problem"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The clique problem is one of the most well-known NP-complete problems. Under some simplification it can be formulated as follows. Consider an undirected graph "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":". It is required to find a subset of vertices "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the maximum size such that any two of them are connected by an edge in graph "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":". Sounds simple, doesn't it? Nobody yet knows an algorithm that finds a solution to this problem in polynomial time of the size of the graph. However, as with many other NP-complete problems, the clique problem is easier if you consider a specific type of a graph."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" distinct points on a line. Let the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th point have the coordinate "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xi"},{"kind":"text","text":" and weight "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"wi"},{"kind":"text","text":". Let's form graph "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":", whose vertices are these points and edges connect exactly the pairs of points "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(i, j)"},{"kind":"text","text":", such that the distance between them is not less than the sum of their weights, or more formally: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"|xi - xj| ≥ wi + wj"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find the size of the maximum clique in such graph."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains the integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 200 000"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of points."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contains two numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xi"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"wi"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ xi ≤ 109, 1 ≤ wi ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the coordinate and the weight of a point. All "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xi"},{"kind":"text","text":" are different."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single number — the number of vertexes in the maximum clique of the given graph."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n2 3\n3 1\n6 1\n0 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If you happen to know how to solve this problem without using the specific properties of the graph formulated in the problem statement, then you are able to get a prize of one million dollars!"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The picture for the sample test."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/0a8c06923497c004271bd233089f67784b07aa282bb72b78ada1ac395fec1ebb.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"527D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/527/problem/D"}